        "zh-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "47cce5f6-5e81-3bdd-871f-3cb99bd7a10e",
                "word": "misogyny",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "en",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "e871b6b0-cf5a-489c-b759-2fec4baeea1e",
                        "entry_id": "47cce5f6-5e81-3bdd-871f-3cb99bd7a10e",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "misogynies"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "127a6a1c-75d0-39e2-abc2-3f3df2d9445a",
                        "entry_id": "47cce5f6-5e81-3bdd-871f-3cb99bd7a10e",
                        "glosses": [
                            "厭女，厭女症，厭惡女人"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cedf9c04-4ec8-417c-a99c-57349ff80520",
                                "sense_id": "127a6a1c-75d0-39e2-abc2-3f3df2d9445a",
                                "text": "儘管她反對將偏見的類型簡單化地混為一談，但她認為厭女症通常存在於自戀和強迫性的反猶太偏見中。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "0be8ad49-f455-46ba-a3e0-02f4e4f009b7",
                                "sense_id": "127a6a1c-75d0-39e2-abc2-3f3df2d9445a",
                                "text": "His misogyny, like that of his predecessors, is more than prejudice; […]",
                                "translation": "他的厭女症，就像他的前輩一樣，不僅僅是偏見； […]"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "bbf10a22-3524-42d1-9f68-8b2b7fc7782b",
                                "sense_id": "127a6a1c-75d0-39e2-abc2-3f3df2d9445a",
                                "text": "This ontological symbiosis also explains his misogyny. By envying Sue, as the man he cannot become, he projects his self-loathing onto her, trying to diminish what he actually admires.",
                                "translation": "這種本體論的共生關係也解釋了他的厭女症。通過羨慕蘇，作為他不能成為的人，他把他的自我厭惡投射到她身上，試圖削弱他實際欽佩的東西。"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "18cd1969-deec-4d29-a855-85e08dac7734",
                                "sense_id": "127a6a1c-75d0-39e2-abc2-3f3df2d9445a",
                                "text": "[…] I have always found it hard that Hamlet, a character that I love and admire, is guilty of a puerile misogyny and, perhaps, more worryingly, of the unnecessary deaths of his old friends from university, Rosencrantz and Guildenstern. When I played him, I could find reasons for the misogyny but half-ignored the murders.",
                                "translation": "[…] 我一直認為，哈姆雷特這個我喜愛和欽佩的人物，犯了愚蠢的厭女症，也許更令人擔憂的是，他大學時的老朋友羅森格蘭茲和吉爾登斯吞的無謂死亡。當我扮演他時，我可以為厭女症找到理由，但對謀殺案卻半點不以為然。"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
